# 3D / Spatial UI

Use perspective, layered planes, and depth-aware product presentation while keeping a complete two-dimensional interaction path.

- **Palette:** Light background `#EEF2FF`, foreground `#111827`, primary `#4F46E5`, accent `#0EA5E9`, surface `#FFFFFF`, border `#C7D2FE`, focus `#3730A3`. Dark background `#080B18`, foreground `#F8FAFC`, surface `#151A2E`, primary `#A5B4FC`, accent `#38BDF8`.
- **Type:** Geometric sans with clear depth-independent labels. Text stays on a flat readable plane and never follows extreme perspective.
- **Surfaces:** Layered elevation, restrained perspective, light/shadow cues, transform-based tilt, and occasional product scene. Shared tokens define z-depth as well as shadows.
- **Components:** Product cards can tilt; forms, menus, tables, dialogs, and checkout controls remain two-dimensional. Any interactive object has a standard button/list alternative.
- **Interaction:** Pointer tilt or rotation is optional, bounded, and resets predictably. Keyboard focus never moves in 3D. Focus is a stable ring; disabled states stop spatial reactions.
- **Responsive:** Disable or greatly reduce perspective on touch and small screens, flatten overlapping planes, and keep important content in DOM order.
- **Accessibility:** Provide names, text equivalents, non-drag controls, and a complete 2D path. Never encode navigation in spatial position alone; avoid motion that triggers vestibular discomfort.
- **Theme/performance:** Both themes tune lighting separately. CSS transforms are default; lazy-load optional 3D and never require WebGL for ordinary screens. Pause offscreen scenes, preserve layout dimensions, and honor reduced motion/data.

Representative preview: product showcase with one optional tilt model, flat specification cards, comparison table, and conventional purchase action.
